"""A signed spelling cue at token boundaries involving y.

Splitting 'you...' after y gives the largest negative prediction; other
rounded-vowel continuations give smaller ones. Some familiar y-word
families have the opposite sign. There is a small one-piece after-effect,
and a separate positive cue for 'of you'. Thai y+vowel marks and the
Japanese continuations yu-u and yo-ro receive small negative predictions.
A document begins at a small positive baseline, then returns near zero.
These rules omit most lexical and background variation.
